    "narrative": "The LawDog starting lineup for 2026-07-02 centers around **Jonathan Aranda**, our strongest play of the day with a 70.47 efficiency score. **Jonathan Aranda** benefits from a high-leverage #2 spot in the order against a beatable arm in Kolek, combined with favorable wind conditions that boost his power potential. **Bryson Stott** (62.94) and **Masyn Winn** (60.61) also register as strong starts, with **Masyn Winn** particularly interesting given the aggressive 7.82 xERA of the opposing starter, Waldrep. While **Cal Raleigh** (57.53) sits just below our threshold for a \"Strong\" start, his presence behind the plate remains vital, though his matchup against Ure\u00f1a is slightly hampered by a platoon disadvantage.\n\nOur most difficult decision involved **Gavin Sheets**, who narrowly missed the 60-point threshold for an elite start, landing at 59.70. While the \"Lineup Pending\" status introduces volatility, the projection assumes an aggressive #2 slot against Roki Sasaki. We opted to keep **Gavin Sheets** in the active lineup because his dynamic platoon advantage against the right-handed Sasaki outweighs the risk of the pending lineup confirmation. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** sidelined on the IL, and **Lawrence Butler** and **Geraldo Perdomo** unavailable due to team off-days, our depth is tested. We are holding reserves like **Daulton Varsho**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Taylor Ward**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Matt Chapman**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Drew Gilbert** in anticipation of the full slate tomorrow. Monitor the weather reports closely for the **Gavin Sheets** start, as any late-breaking wind shifts could neutralize his current edge.",
